WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.359
It was a busy day at Metro City Central Bank.

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.211
"I need some money," a customer said.

3
00:00:09.212 --> 00:00:11.654
The bank teller typed on a computer.

4
00:00:11.655 --> 00:00:14.223
A drawer popped open.

5
00:00:14.224 --> 00:00:16.857
"Uh-oh," the bank teller said.

6
00:00:16.858 --> 00:00:19.849
"There's no more money in the drawer.

7
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:23.794
Wait here. I'll get it from the safe."

8
00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:27.566
He went over to the safe, unlocked the door, and opened it.

9
00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:34.624
The bank teller gasped. "All the money is gone!"

10
00:00:34.625 --> 00:00:39.857
*** "Wow!" Mara said. "Saturn's rings are

11
00:00:39.858 --> 00:00:43.000
amazing." Roxy and her friends were in the computer center at

12
00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:45.878
school. They were doing research projects for

13
00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:50.080
science. "I'd like to run around Saturn on its rings," Jack

14
00:00:50.081 --> 00:00:55.444
said. Mara rolled her eyes. "You can't run on Saturn's rings,

15
00:00:55.445 --> 00:01:01.792
Jack. They're not solid. They're made of chunks of ice and rock that float around the

16
00:01:01.793 --> 00:01:03.988
planet." Terrell looked over from his

17
00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:06.867
computer. "I'm researching the first moon

18
00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:09.476
landing. You could definitely run on the

19
00:01:09.477 --> 00:01:11.814
moon. You'd need a spacesuit

20
00:01:11.815 --> 00:01:16.112
though." Roxy nodded. "Plus, there isn't much gravity on the

21
00:01:16.113 --> 00:01:19.014
moon. So you could jump really

22
00:01:19.015 --> 00:01:22.800
high." Jack stood up. "Earth, this is Astronaut

23
00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.930
Jack. I just landed on the

24
00:01:24.931 --> 00:01:27.588
moon. I'm going to try moon jumping

25
00:01:27.589 --> 00:01:29.622
now!" Jack jumped as high as he

26
00:01:29.623 --> 00:01:33.986
could. Roxy, Mara, and Terrell laughed.

27
00:01:33.987 --> 00:01:35.922
Miss Apricot walked over.

28
00:01:35.923 --> 00:01:40.592
"Jack, did you pick a topic for your project yet?"

29
00:01:40.593 --> 00:01:45.021
Jack scratched his head. "Uh, I might research aliens."

30
00:01:45.022 --> 00:01:46.893
Miss Apricot sighed.

31
00:01:46.894 --> 00:01:51.339
"Please pick something more serious than that.

32
00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:54.214
And stop jumping."

33
00:01:54.215 --> 00:01:57.626
"Okay, Miss Apricot." Jack sat back down.

34
00:01:57.627 --> 00:02:01.421
"What are you writing about, Roxy?" Terrell asked.

35
00:02:01.422 --> 00:02:05.296
"Well," Roxy said. "I picked the planet Mercury.

36
00:02:05.297 --> 00:02:07.730
But it's not very interesting."

37
00:02:07.731 --> 00:02:10.101
Terrell looked thoughtful for a moment.

38
00:02:10.102 --> 00:02:14.300
"I have an idea—Rocket Girl."

39
00:02:14.301 --> 00:02:18.068
Roxy tried not to laugh. She knew Terrell was kidding.

40
00:02:18.069 --> 00:02:19.991
"Very funny, Terrell.

41
00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:24.089
But Rocket Girl has more important things to do than help me."

42
00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.641
Terrell shook his head.

43
00:02:25.642 --> 00:02:29.332
"No, I meant you should write about Rocket Girl.

44
00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:31.660
She can fly through space, right?

45
00:02:31.661 --> 00:02:34.956
And she's probably as fast as a comet."

46
00:02:34.957 --> 00:02:39.874
Mara chuckled. "That's ridiculous, Terrell!"

47
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:44.272
"It's even sillier than my alien idea!" Jack said.

48
00:02:44.273 --> 00:02:48.378
Just then Roxy's watch beeped.

49
00:02:48.379 --> 00:02:51.014
"I'll be right back," she whispered to Terrell.

50
00:02:51.015 --> 00:02:53.659
"Mayor Bloom is calling me."

51
00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.207
Roxy stepped out of the computer center.

52
00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:59.183
"Mayor Bloom, what's wrong?"

53
00:02:59.184 --> 00:03:02.586
"I need your help, Rocket Girl!" Mayor Bloom said.

54
00:03:02.587 --> 00:03:06.070
"Metro City Central Bank was just robbed."

55
00:03:06.071 --> 00:03:08.207
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

56
00:03:08.208 --> 00:03:11.776
"I'll be there right away!"

